      "notes": "Conditional numerical parity reproduces K0, K0_prime and both error values at published printed precision, with V0 held fixed. V0=154.5678863704812 A^3 per conventional Fe3C cell (Z=4) is adopted from the Figure 1 full-range calculated curve; it is not a printed or author-confirmed reference volume. Published K coefficients and errors are preserved. The source confidence convention, original fit inputs, weighting and fixed/free V0 choice remain unconfirmed. Matching conditional residual-based errors does not establish the original experimental uncertainty calculation, author-workflow reproduction or a physical-validation/recommendation claim. The reconstruction uses all 22 digitized Figure 1 markers, including the ambient marker, with equal pressure weights and adopted V0 fixed. K0 and K0_prime are free. Covariance is inverse(J^T J) times SSE/(22-2); its errors condition on exact V0 and omit V0 uncertainty. The result is K0=160.757426 +/-2.353365 GPa and K0_prime=5.942125 +/-0.219843, which round to 161+/-2 and 5.9+/-0.2. Digitization/calibration errors are correlated and original experimental errors are unknown. The 19 final Table S1 rows remain a separate complete numeric dataset; three graph markers are absent from it. Published low/high split fits are retained only in the research audit, not offered as public EOS records. The main text rounds the upper limit to 47 GPa; Table S1 reaches 47.4 GPa. The nominal split ranges do not establish separate structural phases or a phase-stability envelope.",
