      "pressure_range_status": "reported_exactly",
      "determination_method": "experimental",
      "record_kind": "published",
      "notes": "Conditional parameter parity compares K0 and K0_prime within the printed source error widths using all 12 nonambient Table 1 observations. Measured V0=155.28(11) A^3 per conventional Pnma Fe3C cell (Z=4) is fixed as in the source, not independently recovered by the fit. Published errors have unspecified confidence. The diagnostic effective-variance objective treats printed pressure and volume widths as if independent standard errors; its unscaled inverse-JtJ covariance is conditional. Original residual direction, weights, covariance, confidence convention and fit project are unavailable. Fixed-V0 uncertainty and shared calibration errors are not propagated. Original ruby wavelengths and separate ruby/neon pressure arrays are missing, so the pressure averaging cannot be replayed. Original-scale published coefficients and observations are preserved; Litasov (2013) recalibrated comparison coefficients are not substituted. This is not author-workflow reproduction, magnetic-phase validation or a recommendation for extrapolation. Eq. (2) approximates the 1-bar reference by zero pressure. The source is a 300 K isotherm; the 299-301 K range records reported room-temperature variation, not a thermal model. No crystallographic transition was observed to 30.5 GPa; the magnetic state was not measured. The material's structural reference cell is independent of this EOS V0.",
